  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics. I\'m focusing on the core aesthetic: a warm, creamy white background (`#FAF9F6`) optimized for mobile. This means I\'ll need to create a mobile-first design, or consider how to render a nice mock-up/card styled beautifully on high screen resolutions or consider a fluid, elegant, mobile-centric layout. I\'m exploring different rendering options to ensure optimal visual appeal and responsiveness.\n\n\n**Refining the Mockup**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the mobile layout, aiming for pixel-perfect optimization. I\'m oscillating between two approaches: a mobile-first design and a premium mobile mockup. I\'m leaning toward the latter for a polished feel, using a simulated device wrapper on desktop and a full-screen display on mobile. I also have an early plan for a uniform button layout.\n\n\n**Designing the Purple Border**\n\nI\'ve hit on a solution for the button borders: custom SVG overlays. The goal is a hand-drawn brushstroke effect in purple. I\'m exploring SVG paths for a rough square, aiming for a high-end look. I can use an SVG background for each button, with purple stroke and varying path coordinates. I\'m confident this method will perfectly capture the desired aesthetic, using hand-drawn SVG lines to make each square button unique.\n\n\n**Perfecting the SVG Paths**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on the SVG paths for the purple borders. I\'m aiming for an incredibly hand-drawn, sketchy aesthetic, crafting paths that slightly overshoot at the corners and have natural wiggles, or multiple overlapping strokes for authenticity. The goal is to perfectly match the distinct, hand-drawn brushstroke style, with the SVG paths being meticulously written and fine-tuned for an artistic feel. I\'m also now planning to use `aspect-square w-full` to create perfect, uniform squares.\n\n\n**Balancing the Layout**\n\nI\'m now carefully planning the layout to ensure three stacked squares look perfectly balanced on a mobile screen. I\'m focusing on responsive spacing and alignment for visual harmony. Additionally, I\'ve got to consider adding some small, tappable icons to the bottom footer, with a user story icon and an Instagram icon on the left, and a shopping basket icon on the right. I\'m considering using Lucide icons for this. I\'ve also had a great idea: if there\'s a shopping basket, I can create a functional basket count badge and a slide-up drawer or modal to display basket items with checkout options! Also, the user story icon could open a pop-up story feed (similar to Instagram Stories!) to show \"Meet the Artist\" or \"Studio Journal\" slides!\n\n\n**Defining the Sub-Menus**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the sub-menu structure and interactions. I\'m focusing on \"Tapping Photography\" to unveil the \"Nature/Landscapes\" and \"Urban/Culture\" squares. I\'m also now planning for \"Tapping Paintings\" which will reveal a \"Mini, Studio, Statement\" stack. I\'m imagining a clean animation for a fluid, aesthetic transition. I\'ll be using `motion/react` to design this elegant interaction between the main and sub-menus. The final, crucial step: upon selecting a sub-menu square, a gorgeous artwork grid will be revealed. I\'m envisioning the grid with detailed artwork info, along with high-res, visually stunning imagery!\n\n\n**Cataloging the Artwork**\n\nI\'m now carefully cataloging the artwork examples for each sub-menu. I\'m focusing on \"Mini,\" \"Studio,\" and \"Statement\" painting sizes. I\'m defining specific examples for each size, including \"Gilded Petals,\" \"Verdant Echo,\" and \"Metropolis Breath,\" complete with pricing. I\'m also now planning for Photography entries as well. I need to make the artworks fit the grid, so I can display the high-res images with supporting artwork info!\n\n\n**Expanding the Portfolio**\n\nI\'m now generating specific artwork examples for the photography sub-menus. For \"Nature/Landscapes,\" I\'ve added \"Mist of Yosemite,\" \"S\303\263lheimasandur,\" and \"Dune NO. 8.\" For \"Urban/Culture,\" I\'ve included \"Neon Transit,\" \"Facade of Lisbon,\" and \"Rainy Caf\303\251.\" These are all high-quality options for the image grid. I can see the layout now; it\'s getting perfect! Now, I\'m onto the fun part!\n\nI have also considered making the \"Surprise Me!\" button a server-side API call via Gemini, which would allow a personalized recommendation based on user input.\n\n\n**Implementing the Mockup**\n\nI\'m now implementing the 3D floating box frame mockup. I\'m focusing on making it a draggable, tiltable CSS 3D box frame, allowing the user to view the artwork from different angles. I\'m also planning the frame\'s color variations, and the clear price and \"Add to Basket\" button functionality. I\'m prioritizing building a polished, interactive experience. I\'m also considering the integration with the server-side API for personalized artwork generation, focusing on the beautiful simulated artwork view within the frame.\n\n\n\n**Designing the Box Frame**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the 3D floating box frame, with interactive toggles for frame materials: black, white, oak, or no frame. I\'m focusing on realistic wood texturing using CSS, including beveled edges, shadow offsets, and metallic backing. I\'m also implementing the \"Perspective Angles\" toggle, with both a front view and a draggable, tiltable 3D view.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will inspect the existing `package.json` to understand the dependencies and build scripts before editing the files."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 264852630
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
