  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Building the Frontend!**\n\nI\'m moving forward now to build the interactive frontend. I\'ve realized, before I go any further, that I need to establish some good file modeling. Let\'s see: I\'ll start with `/src/types.ts` to declare types cleanly to avoid those massive, complex files that exceed limits!\n\n\n**Defining the Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been defining the data structures needed for the project. I\'ve got `Artwork`, `FrameType`, and `BasketItem` fleshed out, including a few art categories to get us started. I\'m also thinking about laying out elements for the mobile view, like perfect squares for categories, and a hand-drawn purple border.\n\n\n**Creating the `<HandDrawnBox>`**\n\nI\'m now writing the `<HandDrawnBox>` React component. I\'m focusing on rendering a perfect square using Tailwind classes. The goal is to make a hand-drawn SVG overlay, generating sketched paths. I\'ll make sure there are subtle hover animations and brushstroke purple borders (#6A0DAD) with custom SVG filters or overlay effects. The sketching border will be majestic!\n\n\n**Refining the SVG**\n\nI\'m now refining the SVG path for the hand-drawn border, focusing on double strokes with slight offsets to simulate a brush overlay. I\'m adding subtle opacity variations to the strokes for a more realistic effect. The paths are still coming along nicely, but it\'s important to make the hover animation amazing.\n\n\n**Perfecting the SVG Path**\n\nI\'m incredibly excited because the SVG path with its control points is working beautifully. The organic, hand-drawn sketch scales perfectly. I\'m imagining how pristine white squares with a sketchy purple border will look for the Paintings and Photography sub-menus. The sub-category squares will stack beautifully. Clicking an artwork will slide open a detailed Art Details View, and I can\'t wait to see it!\n\n\n**Designing the 3D Mockup**\n\nI\'m now designing the 3D canvas mockup with a focus on interactive frame selection. I\'m visualizing a floating box frame with options: Black, White, Oak, or None, each with unique styling. The goal is a captivating, interactive 3D perspective rotation, likely implemented with CSS transformations and a perspective container. I need to make the frame responsive, and am considering a slider for frame control.\n\n\n**Implementing 3D Rotation**\n\nI\'m now integrating mouse drag interaction for 3D canvas rotation, aiming for intuitive user control. I\'m also planning preset angle toggle buttons for Frontal View and Shadowbox Perspective, supporting both drag/tilt interaction and touch gestures. I\'m aiming for smooth transitions for a premium experience. I need to make the mockup realistically beautiful.\n\nI am working on the aesthetics now. I am focusing on detailed framing: a border representing the frame mouldings (e.g., `border-[12px] border-slate-900` for black), with an inner recessed gap (`bg-black/30 w-full h-full p-2`). Inside the recessed frame, I\'ll make the canvas \"float\" with a tiny black shadow dropcast beneath it: `box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.4)`. Also, I\'ll make the canvas have thickness to look like a true stretched canvas, which I\'ll represent with beautiful perspective side layers of gradient shadows.\n\n\n**Developing the Artwork Canvas**\n\nI\'m now deeply engrossed in building the `<ArtworkCanvas>` component. I\'m focusing on providing options for both generative art and photo layouts. I\'m imagining how stunning it will look. I\'ll make the paintings have generative, custom designs, and have a texture overlay. This will all be so elegant.\n\n\n"
