  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Dynamic Artwork**\n\nI\'ve made progress on the data structure, and am now moving to component design and coding. The focus is on a stunning `<ArtworkCanvas>` component to manage the dynamic artwork representations on screen. It is designed to generate drawings based on primary, secondary, and tertiary colors, and also `visualType`.\n\n\n**Refining Generative Techniques**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the SVG implementation within the `<ArtworkCanvas>` component. The key is using SVG to create resilient, scalable generative art. I\'m exploring how to draw stylized graphics using primary, secondary, and tertiary colors via SVG elements. This approach promises excellent responsiveness, even under 3D transformations, a significant advantage over raster-based alternatives.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Types**\n\nI\'ve been defining the visual types for the dynamic artwork. For geometric visuals, I\'m thinking of mid-century overlapping shapes. Cosmic visuals will blend gradients and glowing bubbles. Fluid types will incorporate curved waves and organic blobs. Botanical designs will feature leaf veins and charcoal branches. Minimalist styles involve a bold disc against a gesso background. I\'m excited about the diversity this approach offers.\n\n\n**Adding Image Enhancement**\n\nI\'m now integrating high-resolution, curated images from Picsum or Unsplash, styled with an analog photographic film border and subtle grain for a gallery treatment. I\'m focusing on robust `<img>` element implementation using `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` to enhance visual appeal and data management. I\'m building a themed library of copyright-free images, with fallbacks to beautiful Picsum IDs. An example includes a perfect Yosemite image fetched from Unsplash.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/ArtworkCanvas.tsx`. This component handles rendering the actual visual art inside our 3D frames. For Paintings (and AI surprise curations), it creates dynamic vector-art abstract shapes (drawn with organic CSS filters and texture masks) matching the curation\'s hex palettes. For Photography, it loads high-contrast archival images from professional fine-art source repositories, blended with an artistic matte paper texture overlay."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 793703647
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
