  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing 3D Frame Mockup**\n\nI\'ve made excellent progress. The `ArtworkCanvas` component is complete and aesthetically pleasing. I\'m now focused on developing the interactive 3D Frame Mockup Component. I need to figure out what\'s required for the floating 3D frame mockup inside the applet. It will use React hook state.\n\n\n**Defining Frame Material Options**\n\nI\'m now determining the frame materials users can select: Black, White, Oak, or None (gallery wrap). My aim is a realistic shadowbox display, including a 3D rotation option. Initially, I will implement \"front\" and \"tilt\" views, the latter having a beautiful rotated perspective. I\'m focusing now on building an interactive pointer drag for canvas rotation, using onPointer events to create a native 3D model interaction. I\'m exploring the \"None\" frame style (gallery wrap) shadowbox, considering how to draw a 3D border edge with a deep canvas block.\n\n\n**Refining Frame Style Details**\n\nI\'ve been iterating on the frame material styles, focusing on realistic shadowbox representations. The \"Black\" and \"White\" options are now well-defined, and the Oak frame is close to completion. I\'m experimenting with CSS for the deep \"recess gap\" effect to create a believable floating canvas appearance. I\'m exploring shadow and border variations for more visual depth, and now writing an elegant CSS implementation of the oak woodgrain. I\'m striving for aesthetically pleasing representations for each material type.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the interactive `/src/components/ThreeDFrameMockup.tsx` component. It implements a complete physical shadowbox simulator using CSS 3D matrix-perspective spaces. Users can toggle frame variants (Charcoal Black, Gilded Oak, Matte White, or Raw Canvas) and click-drag or drag-swipe directly over the canvas to tilt, spin, and rotate the framed composition in responsive 3D space, showing realistic side depth profiles."
